  "description": "Tender baby spinach and red shen choy are briefly simmered just until wilted, then served very simply in a broth flavored with lightly browned garlic. I can't think of an easier way to put a delicious side dish on the table.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: vegetable oil → canola oil or peanut oil; low-sodium chicken stock → vegetable stock\n\nNotes: Shen choy is also known as red amaranth and can be found in most Asian markets. If unavailable, you can use more spinach or any semi-tender green like watercress, iceberg lettuce, or snow pea shoots.",
